1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm
/F1 16 Tf
(Project Charter: Beacon Migration) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Project Sponsor: VP of Engineering, Dana Reyes) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Project Lead: Priya Nadella) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Start Date: February 2, 2026    Target Completion: May 29, 2026) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(1. Background) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The Beacon service currently runs on a decommissioned internal hosting platform that) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(reaches end-of-life support in Q3 2026. This charter authorizes the migration of Beacon to) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(the company's standard Kubernetes platform before that deadline.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(2. Objectives) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Migrate all Beacon workloads to Kubernetes with zero data loss, reduce monthly) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(infrastructure cost by at least 20 percent, and establish automated deployment pipelines) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(so future releases no longer require manual server provisioning.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(3. Scope) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(In scope: the Beacon API service, its PostgreSQL database, and the nightly batch reporting) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(job. Out of scope: the Beacon mobile app, which is managed by a separate team and has no) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(infrastructure dependency on this migration.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(4. Milestones) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Milestone 1 \(Feb 20\): staging environment fully migrated and passing smoke tests.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Milestone 2 \(Mar 31\): production database replicated with less than 5 minutes of) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(replication lag. Milestone 3 \(Apr 30\): production traffic cut over behind a feature flag.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Milestone 4 \(May 29\): legacy platform decommissioned.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(5. Risks) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The primary risk is data drift during the cutover window. This is mitigated by running) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(dual writes to both the old and new database for a two-week validation period before the) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(legacy database is retired. A secondary risk is unfamiliarity with Kubernetes among the) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(on-call rotation, mitigated by mandatory training completed before Milestone 3.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(6. Approval) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(This charter requires sign-off from the VP of Engineering, the Head of Infrastructure, and) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(the Beacon service owner before work begins.) Tj
T*
ET
